From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-22)
Subject: 0515 sweet_nub: load the device stack, because its classes are not registered yet

The 2026-11-22 01:55 boot (image build/carplay-0511/composite, kernel 0511) settled the S2
question with a number instead of a theory:

  [    0.192] SWEET NUB: probe deferred by 10 s
  [   10.190] SWEET NUB: IOUSBDeviceController metaclass 0
  [   10.190] SWEET NUB: class not registered yet; S2 skipped

C0 itself passed on that boot (C0a/C0b/C0c/C0d, twelve NTBs each parsed to >0 frames), so the
kernel, the gadget and the parser are fine. What fails is kext instantiation: the boot KC parser
creates OSKext objects for the prelinked kexts, but their start routines -- the code that actually
registers the OSMetaClasses -- run only when the kext is loaded. Nothing asks for
IOUSBDeviceFamily before a controller exists, and the personality we need is in that same kext, so
the wait can never resolve itself.

0515 calls OSKext::loadKextWithIdentifier() for IOUSBDeviceFamily, AppleUSBDeviceMux and
AppleUSBDeviceNCM before the lookup, logging each OSReturn. Only then can the metaclass exist and
the vtable/start path be exercised.

--- a/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include <IOKit/IOPlatformExpert.h>
 #include <libkern/c++/OSArray.h>
 #include <libkern/c++/OSDictionary.h>
+#include <libkern/c++/OSKext.h>
 #include <libkern/c++/OSMetaClass.h>
 #include <libkern/c++/OSNumber.h>
 #include <libkern/c++/OSString.h>
@@ -152,6 +153,24 @@
 		printf("SWEET NUB: cannot intern the class name\n");
 		return;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * 0515: the first real boot proved the classes are not registered at T+10 s
+	 * ("SWEET NUB: IOUSBDeviceController metaclass 0" at 10.190 s). Prelinked kexts are only
+	 * *instantiated* by the boot KC parser; their start routines -- which is what registers the
+	 * OSMetaClasses -- run when the kext is loaded. Nothing in a stock system asks for
+	 * IOUSBDeviceFamily until a USB device controller exists, and the personality we rely on lives
+	 * in that same kext, so waiting can never resolve itself. Load the device stack explicitly.
+	 */
+	static const char *device_stack[] = {
+		"com.apple.iokit.IOUSBDeviceFamily",
+		"com.apple.driver.AppleUSBDeviceMux",
+		"com.apple.driver.AppleUSBDeviceNCM",
+	};
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(device_stack) / sizeof(device_stack[0]); i++) {
+		OSReturn loaded = OSKext::loadKextWithIdentifier(device_stack[i]);
+		printf("SWEET NUB: load %s -> 0x%x\n", device_stack[i], loaded);
+	}
+
 	const OSMetaClass *mc = OSMetaClass::getMetaClassWithName(name);
 	printf("SWEET NUB: %s metaclass %p\n", SWEET_NUB_CLASS, mc);
 	if (mc == NULL) {
